    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-10",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 After subsection 45A(3)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-1-sec-10"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00006\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 6, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Unexplained Wealth and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\n\nRestraining orders made after application for unexplained wealth\norder\n\n(3A) A *restraining order made under section 20A ceases to be in force\nif:\n\n(a) the restraining order was made at the same time as or after an\napplication for an *unexplained wealth order is made in\nrelation to the *suspect to whom the restraining order relates;\nand\n\n(b) the court refuses to make either:\n\n(i) a *preliminary unexplained wealth order in connection\nwith the application for the unexplained wealth order; or\n\n(ii) the unexplained wealth order itself; and\n\n(c) one of the following applies:\n\n(i) the time for an appeal against the refusal has expired\nwithout an appeal being lodged;\n\n(ii) an appeal against the refusal has lapsed;\n\n(iii) an appeal against the refusal has been dismissed and\nfinally disposed of.\n\n(3B) A *restraining order made under section 20A ceases to be in force\nif:\n\n(a) the restraining order was made at the same time as or after an\napplication for an *unexplained wealth order is made in\nrelation to the *suspect to whom the restraining order relates;\nand\n\n(b) the court makes the unexplained wealth order (whether\nbefore or after the restraining order was made or applied for);\nand\n\n(c) either:\n\n(i) the unexplained wealth order is complied with; or\n\n(ii) an appeal against the unexplained wealth order has been\nupheld and finally disposed of.",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00006\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 6, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Unexplained Wealth and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\n\nRestraining orders made after application for unexplained wealth\norder\n\n(3A) A *restraining order made under section 20A ceases to be in force\nif:\n\n(a) the restraining order was made at the same time as or after an\napplication for an *unexplained wealth order is made in\nrelation to the *suspect to whom the restraining order relates;\nand\n\n(b) the court refuses to make either:\n\n(i) a *preliminary unexplained wealth order in connection\nwith the application for the unexplained wealth order; or\n\n(ii) the unexplained wealth order itself; and\n\n(c) one of the following applies:\n\n(i) the time for an appeal against the refusal has expired\nwithout an appeal being lodged;\n\n(ii) an appeal against the refusal has lapsed;\n\n(iii) an appeal against the refusal has been dismissed and\nfinally disposed of.\n\n(3B) A *restraining order made under section 20A ceases to be in force\nif:\n\n(a) the restraining order was made at the same time as or after an\napplication for an *unexplained wealth order is made in\nrelation to the *suspect to whom the restraining order relates;\nand\n\n(b) the court makes the unexplained wealth order (whether\nbefore or after the restraining order was made or applied for);\nand\n\n(c) either:\n\n(i) the unexplained wealth order is complied with; or\n\n(ii) an appeal against the unexplained wealth order has been\nupheld and finally disposed of.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-10-ss-3a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-10-ss-3b"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1c5f057e65947d69d5e667d8861b6f0a3208bfb73fedbe35d03a6ee8abccc552"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-1-sec-10",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 After subsection 45A(3)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00006\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 6, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Unexplained Wealth and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\n\nRestraining orders made after application for unexplained wealth\norder\n\n(3A) A *restraining order made under section 20A ceases to be in force\nif:\n\n(a) the restraining order was made at the same time as or after an\napplication for an *unexplained wealth order is made in\nrelation to the *suspect to whom the restraining order relates;\nand\n\n(b) the court refuses to make either:\n\n(i) a *preliminary unexplained wealth order in connection\nwith the application for the unexplained wealth order; or\n\n(ii) the unexplained wealth order itself; and\n\n(c) one of the following applies:\n\n(i) the time for an appeal against the refusal has expired\nwithout an appeal being lodged;\n\n(ii) an appeal against the refusal has lapsed;\n\n(iii) an appeal against the refusal has been dismissed and\nfinally disposed of.\n\n(3B) A *restraining order made under section 20A ceases to be in force\nif:\n\n(a) the restraining order was made at the same time as or after an\napplication for an *unexplained wealth order is made in\nrelation to the *suspect to whom the restraining order relates;\nand\n\n(b) the court makes the unexplained wealth order (whether\nbefore or after the restraining order was made or applied for);\nand\n\n(c) either:\n\n(i) the unexplained wealth order is complied with; or\n\n(ii) an appeal against the unexplained wealth order has been\nupheld and finally disposed of."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-10-ss-3a",
