    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-15",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15 Subsection 179B(2)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-1-sec-15"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nEffect of restraining orders\n\n(1A) Paragraphs (1)(b) and (c) do not apply if a *restraining order made\nunder section 20A in relation to the person:\n\n(a) is in force; or\n\n(b) has been revoked under section 44.\n\n(1B) If subsection (1A) applies, the court may, in considering making an\norder under subsection (1), take into account:\n\n(a) an affidavit of an *authorised officer that:\n\n(i) supported the application for the *restraining order made\nunder section 20A; and\n\n(ii) met the requirements of subsection 20A(3); and\n\n(b) any material that an authorised officer or *proceeds of crime\nauthority provided, in the proceedings under section 20A,\nrelating to the requirements of subsection 20A(3); and\n\n(c) any other material that an authorised officer or proceeds of\ncrime authority provides in the proceedings under this\nsection.\nThis subsection does not limit the court’s power to take other\nmaterial into account.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00006\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 6, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Unexplained Wealth and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\n\nAffidavit requirements\n\n(2) An application for an *unexplained wealth order in relation to a\nperson must be supported by an affidavit of an *authorised officer\nthat:\n\n(a) states that the authorised officer suspects that the person’s\n*total wealth exceeds the value of the person’s *wealth that\nwas *lawfully acquired; and\n\n(b) includes the grounds on which the authorised officer holds\nthat suspicion.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nEffect of restraining orders\n\n(1A) Paragraphs (1)(b) and (c) do not apply if a *restraining order made\nunder section 20A in relation to the person:\n\n(a) is in force; or\n\n(b) has been revoked under section 44.\n\n(1B) If subsection (1A) applies, the court may, in considering making an\norder under subsection (1), take into account:\n\n(a) an affidavit of an *authorised officer that:\n\n(i) supported the application for the *restraining order made\nunder section 20A; and\n\n(ii) met the requirements of subsection 20A(3); and\n\n(b) any material that an authorised officer or *proceeds of crime\nauthority provided, in the proceedings under section 20A,\nrelating to the requirements of subsection 20A(3); and\n\n(c) any other material that an authorised officer or proceeds of\ncrime authority provides in the proceedings under this\nsection.\nThis subsection does not limit the court’s power to take other\nmaterial into account.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00006\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 6, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Unexplained Wealth and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\n\nAffidavit requirements\n\n(2) An application for an *unexplained wealth order in relation to a\nperson must be supported by an affidavit of an *authorised officer\nthat:\n\n(a) states that the authorised officer suspects that the person’s\n*total wealth exceeds the value of the person’s *wealth that\nwas *lawfully acquired; and\n\n(b) includes the grounds on which the authorised officer holds\nthat suspicion.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-15-ss-1a"
        },
