    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-17",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "17 At the end of section 179B",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-1-sec-17"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.11",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\nRefusal to make preliminary unexplained wealth order\n\n(4) Despite subsection (1), the court may refuse to make the\n*preliminary unexplained wealth order if the court is satisfied that\nthere are not reasonable grounds to suspect that the person’s *total\nwealth exceeds by $100,000 or more the value of the person’s\n*wealth that was *lawfully acquired.",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\nRefusal to make preliminary unexplained wealth order\n\n(4) Despite subsection (1), the court may refuse to make the\n*preliminary unexplained wealth order if the court is satisfied that\nthere are not reasonable grounds to suspect that the person’s *total\nwealth exceeds by $100,000 or more the value of the person’s\n*wealth that was *lawfully acquired.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-17-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-17-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7f03391800651db26054e51e80ae622e66e2d662146e2d99961d2d15957f7c69",
      "skos:note": "Court may refuse to make preliminary unexplained wealth order if no reasonable grounds exist."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-1-sec-17",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "17 At the end of section 179B",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 11,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\nRefusal to make preliminary unexplained wealth order\n\n(4) Despite subsection (1), the court may refuse to make the\n*preliminary unexplained wealth order if the court is satisfied that\nthere are not reasonable grounds to suspect that the person’s *total\nwealth exceeds by $100,000 or more the value of the person’s\n*wealth that was *lawfully acquired."
    },
