    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-19",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19 Subsection 179E(4)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-1-sec-19"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.11",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(4) To avoid doubt:\n\n(a) when considering whether to make an order under\nsubsection (1), the court may have regard to information not\nincluded in the application; and\n\n(b) the court may make an order under subsection (1) in relation\nto a person even if the person failed to appear as required by\nthe *preliminary unexplained wealth order.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00006\n\nSchedule 1  Unexplained wealth\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Unexplained Wealth and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\nNo. 6, 2015",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(4) To avoid doubt:\n\n(a) when considering whether to make an order under\nsubsection (1), the court may have regard to information not\nincluded in the application; and\n\n(b) the court may make an order under subsection (1) in relation\nto a person even if the person failed to appear as required by\nthe *preliminary unexplained wealth order.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00006\n\nSchedule 1  Unexplained wealth\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Unexplained Wealth and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\nNo. 6, 2015",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-19-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9367e7f6db46edcd4b780c86ccc616bc6968a5e729b42df4372a7584b1f5ecae",
      "skos:note": "Court may consider information not included in application when making an order under subsection (1)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-1-sec-19",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19 Subsection 179E(4)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 11,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(4) To avoid doubt:\n\n(a) when considering whether to make an order under\nsubsection (1), the court may have regard to information not\nincluded in the application; and\n\n(b) the court may make an order under subsection (1) in relation\nto a person even if the person failed to appear as required by\nthe *preliminary unexplained wealth order.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00006\n\nSchedule 1  Unexplained wealth\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Unexplained Wealth and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\nNo. 6, 2015"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-19-norm",
