    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-179sb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "179SB Charges may be registered",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-1-sec-179sb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.14",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a charge is created by section 179SA on property of a\nparticular kind; and\n\n(b) the provisions of any law of the Commonwealth or of a State\nor Territory provide for the registration of title to, or charges\nover, property of that kind;\nthe *Official Trustee or the *responsible authority for the\n*unexplained wealth order or *restraining order referred to in that\nsection may cause the charge so created to be registered under the\nprovisions of that law.\n\n(2) A person who purchases or otherwise acquires an *interest in the\nproperty after the registration of the charge is taken, for the\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00006\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 6, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Unexplained Wealth and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\n\npurposes of paragraph 179SA(2)(d), to have notice of the charge at\nthe time of the purchase or acquisition.\n\n(3) In this section:\nregistration of a charge on a particular kind of personal property\nwithin the meaning of the Personal Property Securities Act 2009\nincludes the registration of data in relation to that kind of property\nfor the purposes of paragraph 148(c) of that Act.\nNote:\nThe Personal Property Securities Act 2009 provides for the\nregistration of such data only if regulations are made for the purposes\nof paragraph 148(c) of that Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a charge is created by section 179SA on property of a\nparticular kind; and\n\n(b) the provisions of any law of the Commonwealth or of a State\nor Territory provide for the registration of title to, or charges\nover, property of that kind;\nthe *Official Trustee or the *responsible authority for the\n*unexplained wealth order or *restraining order referred to in that\nsection may cause the charge so created to be registered under the\nprovisions of that law.\n\n(2) A person who purchases or otherwise acquires an *interest in the\nproperty after the registration of the charge is taken, for the\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00006\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 6, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Unexplained Wealth and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\n\npurposes of paragraph 179SA(2)(d), to have notice of the charge at\nthe time of the purchase or acquisition.\n\n(3) In this section:\nregistration of a charge on a particular kind of personal property\nwithin the meaning of the Personal Property Securities Act 2009\nincludes the registration of data in relation to that kind of property\nfor the purposes of paragraph 148(c) of that Act.\nNote:\nThe Personal Property Securities Act 2009 provides for the\nregistration of such data only if regulations are made for the purposes\nof paragraph 148(c) of that Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-179sb-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-179sb-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-179sb-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5a9b8c833bb35c39e791433699ed51050e211dc776e9bcfd424cd368f8de4c3c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-1-sec-179sb",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "179SB Charges may be registered",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 14,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a charge is created by section 179SA on property of a\nparticular kind; and\n\n(b) the provisions of any law of the Commonwealth or of a State\nor Territory provide for the registration of title to, or charges\nover, property of that kind;\nthe *Official Trustee or the *responsible authority for the\n*unexplained wealth order or *restraining order referred to in that\nsection may cause the charge so created to be registered under the\nprovisions of that law.\n\n(2) A person who purchases or otherwise acquires an *interest in the\nproperty after the registration of the charge is taken, for the\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00006\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\n\nNo. 6, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Unexplained Wealth and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\n\npurposes of paragraph 179SA(2)(d), to have notice of the charge at\nthe time of the purchase or acquisition.\n\n(3) In this section:\nregistration of a charge on a particular kind of personal property\nwithin the meaning of the Personal Property Securities Act 2009\nincludes the registration of data in relation to that kind of property\nfor the purposes of paragraph 148(c) of that Act.\nNote:\nThe Personal Property Securities Act 2009 provides for the\nregistration of such data only if regulations are made for the purposes\nof paragraph 148(c) of that Act."
    },
