    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-26",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26 At the end of section 179U",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-1-sec-26"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.15",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\nReport about unexplained wealth investigations and proceedings\n\n(3) The Commissioner of the Australian Federal Police must give the\nCommittee a report in respect of each financial year that contains\nthe following information:\n\n(a) the number of matters investigated in the year, by each\n*enforcement agency, in respect of which a likely outcome\nmay, or will, be the initiation of proceedings under this Part,\nand the basis for determining that number;\n\n(b) the number and results of applications in the year for:\n\n(i) *restraining orders under section 20A; and\n\n(ii) *unexplained wealth orders;\n\n(c) any other information of a kind prescribed by the regulations.\n\n(4) The report must be given as soon as practicable after the report\nunder section 67 of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979 in\nrespect of the financial year is laid before a House of the\nParliament in accordance with that section.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00006\n\nSchedule 1  Unexplained wealth\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Unexplained Wealth and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\nNo. 6, 2015\n\n(5) If the Commissioner of the Australian Federal Police requests the\n*DPP or the Chief Executive Officer (however described) of an\n*enforcement agency to give the Commissioner information that\nthe Commissioner considers necessary to prepare the report, the\nDPP or Chief Executive Officer must comply with the request.",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\nReport about unexplained wealth investigations and proceedings\n\n(3) The Commissioner of the Australian Federal Police must give the\nCommittee a report in respect of each financial year that contains\nthe following information:\n\n(a) the number of matters investigated in the year, by each\n*enforcement agency, in respect of which a likely outcome\nmay, or will, be the initiation of proceedings under this Part,\nand the basis for determining that number;\n\n(b) the number and results of applications in the year for:\n\n(i) *restraining orders under section 20A; and\n\n(ii) *unexplained wealth orders;\n\n(c) any other information of a kind prescribed by the regulations.\n\n(4) The report must be given as soon as practicable after the report\nunder section 67 of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979 in\nrespect of the financial year is laid before a House of the\nParliament in accordance with that section.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00006\n\nSchedule 1  Unexplained wealth\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Unexplained Wealth and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\nNo. 6, 2015\n\n(5) If the Commissioner of the Australian Federal Police requests the\n*DPP or the Chief Executive Officer (however described) of an\n*enforcement agency to give the Commissioner information that\nthe Commissioner considers necessary to prepare the report, the\nDPP or Chief Executive Officer must comply with the request.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-26-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-26-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-26-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a91b9f6b043bcee25ab5a564f815d4a16115d498edf376a8f8a4aa0a19c59b2c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-1-sec-26",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26 At the end of section 179U",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 15,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\nReport about unexplained wealth investigations and proceedings\n\n(3) The Commissioner of the Australian Federal Police must give the\nCommittee a report in respect of each financial year that contains\nthe following information:\n\n(a) the number of matters investigated in the year, by each\n*enforcement agency, in respect of which a likely outcome\nmay, or will, be the initiation of proceedings under this Part,\nand the basis for determining that number;\n\n(b) the number and results of applications in the year for:\n\n(i) *restraining orders under section 20A; and\n\n(ii) *unexplained wealth orders;\n\n(c) any other information of a kind prescribed by the regulations.\n\n(4) The report must be given as soon as practicable after the report\nunder section 67 of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979 in\nrespect of the financial year is laid before a House of the\nParliament in accordance with that section.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00006\n\nSchedule 1  Unexplained wealth\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Unexplained Wealth and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\nNo. 6, 2015\n\n(5) If the Commissioner of the Australian Federal Police requests the\n*DPP or the Chief Executive Officer (however described) of an\n*enforcement agency to give the Commissioner information that\nthe Commissioner considers necessary to prepare the report, the\nDPP or Chief Executive Officer must comply with the request."
    },
